      "isPredictLevel": true,
      "solution": "- Line 1: True and False → False — and needs both sides true; one is false.\n- Line 2: True or False → True — or needs just one side true.\n- Line 3: not False → True — not flips the value.\n- Line 4: True and True → True — both sides true, so and is satisfied.\n- Line 5: False and False → False — neither side true, and still fails.\n- Line 6: False or False → False — neither side true, or has nothing to catch.\n- Line 7: True or True → True — either side alone would do; both happen to be true.\n\nLikely surprises to watch for (Notice & Wonder):\n- Line 4 — some students expect and of two trues to be “extra true” rather than just True.\n- Line 6 — the one case where or doesn’t rescue the result; a few may expect or to “always lean toward True.”\n- Line 3 — usually intuitive, but a student previewing line-5-style reasoning onto it sometimes overthinks a one-sided flip.",
      "questionType": "freeResponse",
      "placeholderText": "Predict the console output for each line",
      "freeResponseHeight": 50,
